                                                              "summary":  "Damodaran revisits the long-running debate over whether rising interest rates must depress stock prices, examining it through both the discount rate channel and the cash flow channel. He argues that equities have held up in 2026 not because markets are ignoring higher rates, but because earnings forecasts have risen substantially enough to offset the higher discount burden. The piece stresses that the rate-equity relationship is not mechanical ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Â it depends heavily on the economic conditions driving rates higher, sector-level pricing power, and reinvestment dynamics.",
